  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: deaae056f5a3ccf4d8025ecf14452651, type: 3}
  m_Name: BOROBUDUR_01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: NusantaraAR.Runtime::NusantaraAR.ArtifactData
  artifactId: BOROBUDUR_01
  displayName:
    id: Candi Borobudur
    en: Borobudur Temple
  localName: Borobudur
  category: 3
  region:
    id: Magelang, Jawa Tengah
    en: Magelang, Central Java
  era:
    id: Abad ke-9, Wangsa Syailendra
    en: 9th century, Sailendra dynasty
  summary:
    id: "Candi Buddha terbesar di dunia: sembilan tingkat (enam persegi dan tiga
      melingkar) yang dimahkotai stupa induk, disusun dari sekitar 55.000 m\xB3 batu
      andesit tanpa semen. Dindingnya memuat sekitar 2.672 panel relief, dengan 504
      arca Buddha di relung langkan dan di dalam 72 stupa terawang. Model dibuat
      di Blender dari data ukuran bersumber; ukuran yang tidak ditemukan sumbernya
      adalah perkiraan."
    en: "The world's largest Buddhist temple: nine levels (six square and three circular)
      crowned by a main stupa, built from about 55,000 m\xB3 of andesite stone without
      mortar. Its walls carry some 2,672 relief panels, with 504 Buddha statues in
      the balustrade niches and inside 72 perforated stupas. The model was made in
      Blender from sourced dimensions; dimensions without a source are estimates."
  thumbnail: {fileID: 2800000, guid: a4948abd0e7f2054daa9b1c741289e94, type: 3}
  prefab: {fileID: 6392355719623272695, guid: 2df392306c46e0e4383ed8769143e2a8, type: 3}
  specimenOwner: 
  collectionNumber: 
  license: Model Blender milik proyek (dibuat dari data ukuran bersumber)
  measurementNote:
    id: Skala 1:200. Denah 123 x 123 m dan tinggi 35 m sampai puncak stupa induk
      (tanpa chattra) bersumber; tinggi tiap teras, diameter teras melingkar, dan
      ukuran stupa adalah perkiraan (lihat Docs/Borobudur_Data.md).
    en: 1:200 scale. The 123 x 123 m plan and the 35 m height to the top of the main
      stupa (without the chattra) are sourced; terrace heights, circular terrace
      diameters and stupa sizes are estimates (see Docs/Borobudur_Data.md).
  markerCode: 58289
  isPlaceholder: 1
  placeholderNote:
    id: 'Model Blender rekonstruksi: relief memakai tekstur bergaya (bukan relief
      asli), arca disederhanakan tanpa mudra, jaladwara dan arca singa belum dimodelkan.
      Akan divalidasi kurator.'
    en: 'Reconstructed Blender model: the reliefs are a stylised texture (not the
      real reliefs), the statues are simplified without mudras, and the water spouts
      and lion statues are not modelled yet. To be validated by a curator.'
  hotspots:
  - hotspotId: kaki
    partName: Kaki
    localPosition: {x: -30, y: 2, z: -60.599995}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Kaki Candi
      en: Temple Base
    regionalTerm: Kamadhatu - alam keinginan
    material:
      id: "Batu andesit (seluruh candi \xB155.000 m\xB3)"
      en: "Andesite stone (\xB155,000 m\xB3 for the whole temple)"
    philosophy:
      id: Kaki candi melambangkan Kamadhatu, alam keinginan - tingkat terbawah dari
        tiga alam dalam kosmologi Buddha yang dilalui peziarah menuju puncak.
      en: The base stands for Kamadhatu, the realm of desire - the lowest of the
        three realms of Buddhist cosmology that pilgrims pass through on their way
        to the top.
    craft:
      id: 'Kaki candi berdenah 123 x 123 m. Kaki yang tampak sekarang adalah kaki
        tambahan: di baliknya tersembunyi kaki asli berhias 160 panel relief Karmawibhangga
        tentang hukum sebab-akibat (karma).'
      en: 'The base measures 123 x 123 m. The base seen today is an added one: behind
        it lies the original base, decorated with 160 Karmavibhangga relief panels
        on the law of cause and effect (karma).'
    history:
      id: Kaki asli ditutup karena cacat struktur yang muncul saat candi masih dibangun.
        Relief tersembunyi itu ditemukan tidak sengaja pada 1885 oleh insinyur Belanda
        Jan Willem IJzerman.
      en: The original base was covered because of structural defects that appeared
        while the temple was being built. The hidden reliefs were discovered by chance
        in 1885 by the Dutch engineer Jan Willem IJzerman.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: 'Kaki candi berdenah 123 x 123 m. Kaki yang tampak sekarang adalah kaki
        tambahan: di baliknya tersembunyi kaki asli berhias 160 panel relief Karmawibhangga
        tentang hukum sebab-akibat (karma).'
      en: 'The base measures 123 x 123 m. The base seen today is an added one: behind
        it lies the original base, decorated with 160 Karmavibhangga relief panels
        on the law of cause and effect (karma).'
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    - Wikipedia Indonesia - Borobudur (id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (01-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: langkan
    partName: Kaki
    localPosition: {x: 32, y: 4.5, z: -60.55}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Langkan & Relung Arca
      en: Balustrades & Buddha Niches
    regionalTerm: Relung arca Dhyani Buddha
    material:
      id: Batu andesit; arca Buddha dipahat dari batu yang sama
      en: Andesite; the Buddha statues are carved from the same stone
    philosophy:
      id: 'Sikap tangan (mudra) arca mengikuti arah mata angin: timur bhumisparsa
        mudra (Aksobya), selatan wara mudra (Ratnasambhawa), barat dhyana mudra (Amitabha),
        utara abhaya mudra (Amoghasiddhi). Di langkan kelima semua arca bersikap
        witarka mudra (Wairocana).'
      en: 'The statues'' hand gestures (mudras) follow the compass: east bhumisparsa
        mudra (Akshobhya), south vara mudra (Ratnasambhava), west dhyana mudra (Amitabha),
        north abhaya mudra (Amoghasiddhi). On the fifth balustrade all statues show
        vitarka mudra (Vairocana).'
    craft:
      id: 'Di atas lima tingkat langkan berderet 432 relung, masing-masing berisi
        arca Buddha duduk: 104, 104, 88, 72, dan 64 relung dari langkan pertama sampai
        kelima. Pada model, relung dan arca disederhanakan.'
      en: 'Along the tops of the five balustrade levels stand 432 niches, each holding
        a seated Buddha: 104, 104, 88, 72 and 64 niches from the first to the fifth
        balustrade. On the model the niches and statues are simplified.'
    history:
      id: Bersama 72 arca di dalam stupa terawang, Borobudur semula memiliki 504
        arca Buddha.
      en: Together with the 72 statues inside the perforated stupas, Borobudur originally
        had 504 Buddha statues.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: 'Di atas lima tingkat langkan berderet 432 relung, masing-masing berisi
        arca Buddha duduk: 104, 104, 88, 72, dan 64 relung dari langkan pertama sampai
        kelima. Pada model, relung dan arca disederhanakan.'
      en: 'Along the tops of the five balustrade levels stand 432 niches, each holding
        a seated Buddha: 104, 104, 88, 72 and 64 niches from the first to the fifth
        balustrade. On the model the niches and statues are simplified.'
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - 'Kompas (13-11-2024) - Arca Candi Borobudur: Jumlah, Jenis, Letak, dan Mitos
      Kunto Bimo (regional.kompas.com)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    - Britannica - Borobudur (britannica.com/topic/Borobudur)
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (01-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: gapura
    partName: Kaki
    localPosition: {x: -1.65, y: 6, z: -61.55}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Tangga & Gapura
      en: Stairways & Gateways
    regionalTerm: Pintu utama di sisi timur
    material:
      id: "Batu andesit (seluruh candi \xB155.000 m\xB3)"
      en: "Andesite stone (\xB155,000 m\xB3 for the whole temple)"
    philosophy:
      id: Peziarah naik dari timur lalu berjalan searah jarum jam (pradaksina) mengelilingi
        setiap tingkat sebelum naik ke tingkat berikutnya - perjalanan simbolis dari
        alam keinginan menuju alam tanpa bentuk.
      en: Pilgrims climb from the east and walk clockwise (pradakshina) around each
        level before going up to the next - a symbolic journey from the realm of
        desire to the formless realm.
    craft:
      id: Tangga naik tepat di tengah keempat sisi candi dan melewati gapura di setiap
        tingkat. Pintu masuk utama berada di sisi timur. Pada model, gapura disederhanakan
        tanpa ukiran kepala kala.
      en: Stairways rise at the centre of all four sides and pass through a gateway
        at every level. The main entrance is on the east side. On the model the gateways
        are simplified, without the carved kala heads.
    history:
      id: Candi ini juga dihiasi 32 arca singa dan 100 jaladwara (pancuran air di
        sudut-sudut), masing-masing jaladwara berukiran unik. Keduanya belum dimodelkan.
      en: The temple is also adorned with 32 lion statues and 100 water spouts at
        the corners, each spout with a unique carving. Neither is modelled yet.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: Tangga naik tepat di tengah keempat sisi candi dan melewati gapura di setiap
        tingkat. Pintu masuk utama berada di sisi timur. Pada model, gapura disederhanakan
        tanpa ukiran kepala kala.
      en: Stairways rise at the centre of all four sides and pass through a gateway
        at every level. The main entrance is on the east side. On the model the gateways
        are simplified, without the carved kala heads.
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (01-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: relief
    partName: Teras1
    localPosition: {x: -20, y: 2.1999998, z: -53.749996}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Relief Lorong
      en: Gallery Reliefs
    regionalTerm: 2.672 panel relief
    material:
      id: Pahatan relief pada batu andesit (tekstur model bergaya, bukan relief asli)
      en: Reliefs carved in andesite (the model uses a stylised texture, not the
        real reliefs)
    philosophy:
      id: Relief dibaca sambil berjalan searah jarum jam. Seri Lalitavistara (120
        panel) mengisahkan hidup Sang Buddha; Jataka dan Avadana mengisahkan kehidupan-kehidupan
        sebelumnya; Gandavyuha (372 panel di lorong 2-4) mengisahkan pengembaraan
        Sudhana mencari kebijaksanaan sampai ia mencapai Kebijaksanaan Sempurna.
      en: The reliefs are read while walking clockwise. The Lalitavistara series
        (120 panels) tells the life of the Buddha; the Jataka and Avadana tell his
        former lives; the Gandavyuha (372 panels in galleries 2-4) follows Sudhana's
        wandering search until he attains Perfect Wisdom.
    craft:
      id: "Borobudur memuat sekitar 2.672 panel relief - 1.460 naratif dan 1.212
        dekoratif - seluas kira-kira 2.500 m\xB2. Relief naratif tersusun dalam 11
        seri sepanjang sekitar 3.000 m di kaki tertutup dan empat lorong pertama."
      en: "Borobudur carries about 2,672 relief panels - 1,460 narrative and 1,212
        decorative - covering some 2,500 m\xB2. The narrative reliefs are arranged
        in 11 series over about 3,000 m on the hidden base and the first four galleries."
    history:
      id: 'Seluruh relief naratif berjumlah 1.460 panel: 160 Karmawibhangga di kaki
        tertutup, 120 Lalitavistara dan 120 Jataka/Avadana di dinding lorong pertama,
        600 Jataka/Avadana di langkan lorong 1-2, dan 372 Gandavyuha.'
      en: 'The narrative reliefs total 1,460 panels: 160 Karmavibhangga on the hidden
        base, 120 Lalitavistara and 120 Jataka/Avadana on the first gallery wall,
        600 Jataka/Avadana on the balustrades of galleries 1-2, and 372 Gandavyuha.'
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: "Borobudur memuat sekitar 2.672 panel relief - 1.460 naratif dan 1.212
        dekoratif - seluas kira-kira 2.500 m\xB2. Relief naratif tersusun dalam 11
        seri sepanjang sekitar 3.000 m di kaki tertutup dan empat lorong pertama."
      en: "Borobudur carries about 2,672 relief panels - 1,460 narrative and 1,212
        decorative - covering some 2,500 m\xB2. The narrative reliefs are arranged
        in 11 series over about 3,000 m on the hidden base and the first four galleries."
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (01-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: andesit
    partName: Teras2
    localPosition: {x: 20, y: 2, z: -50.25}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Batu Andesit Tanpa Semen
      en: Mortarless Andesite
    regionalTerm: 
    material:
      id: "Batu andesit (seluruh candi \xB155.000 m\xB3)"
      en: "Andesite stone (\xB155,000 m\xB3 for the whole temple)"
    philosophy:
      id: 'Proporsi tinggi kaki, badan, dan kepala candi disebut mengikuti rasio
        4 : 6 : 9.'
      en: 'The heights of the base, body and head of the temple are said to follow
        a 4 : 6 : 9 ratio.'
    craft:
      id: Batu andesit dipotong sesuai ukuran, diangkut ke lokasi, lalu disusun tanpa
        semen. Sambungan antarbatu dikunci dengan tonjolan, lekukan, dan pasak ekor
        burung.
      en: The andesite was cut to size, carried to the site and laid without mortar.
        The stones are locked together with knobs, indentations and dovetails.
    history:
      id: Menurut cerita rakyat Jawa, arsiteknya bernama Gunadharma; nama ini tidak
        tercatat dalam prasasti.
      en: According to Javanese folk tales its architect was Gunadharma; the name
        is not recorded in any inscription.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: Batu andesit dipotong sesuai ukuran, diangkut ke lokasi, lalu disusun tanpa
        semen. Sambungan antarbatu dikunci dengan tonjolan, lekukan, dan pasak ekor
        burung.
      en: The andesite was cut to size, carried to the site and laid without mortar.
        The stones are locked together with knobs, indentations and dovetails.
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    - 'F. Musacchio (2025) - Borobudur: A Buddhist mandala in stone (fabriziomusacchio.com)'
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (01-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: rupadhatu
    partName: Teras3
    localPosition: {x: -20, y: 1.9000006, z: -46.75}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Teras Persegi (Rupadhatu)
      en: Square Terraces (Rupadhatu)
    regionalTerm: Rupadhatu - alam berbentuk
    material:
      id: "Batu andesit (seluruh candi \xB155.000 m\xB3)"
      en: "Andesite stone (\xB155,000 m\xB3 for the whole temple)"
    philosophy:
      id: Lima teras persegi (badan candi) melambangkan Rupadhatu, alam berbentuk
        - tingkat tengah di antara alam keinginan (kaki) dan alam tanpa bentuk (puncak).
      en: The five square terraces (the body) stand for Rupadhatu, the world of forms
        - the middle level between the realm of desire (the base) and the formless
        world (the top).
    craft:
      id: Di atas kaki berdiri lima teras persegi yang makin ke atas makin kecil.
        Teras pertama mundur 7 m dari tepi kaki; di antara dinding dan langkan terbentuk
        lorong sempit tempat relief dipahat. Denah sisinya berlekuk-lekuk di sudut.
      en: Above the base stand five square terraces, each smaller than the one below.
        The first terrace is set back 7 m from the edge of the base; between the
        walls and the balustrades run narrow galleries lined with reliefs. The corners
        of the plan are stepped.
    history:
      id: Prasasti Karangtengah (824) menyebut bangunan suci bernama Jinalaya yang
        diresmikan Pramodhawardhani, putri Samaratungga; bangunan ini sering dikaitkan
        dengan Borobudur. Tahap pembangunan kelima diperkirakan selesai sekitar 833.
      en: The Karangtengah inscription (824) mentions a sacred building named Jinalaya
        inaugurated by Pramodhawardhani, daughter of Samaratungga; it is often linked
        to Borobudur. The fifth construction stage is estimated to have been completed
        around 833.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: Di atas kaki berdiri lima teras persegi yang makin ke atas makin kecil.
        Teras pertama mundur 7 m dari tepi kaki; di antara dinding dan langkan terbentuk
        lorong sempit tempat relief dipahat. Denah sisinya berlekuk-lekuk di sudut.
      en: Above the base stand five square terraces, each smaller than the one below.
        The first terrace is set back 7 m from the edge of the base; between the
        walls and the balustrades run narrow galleries lined with reliefs. The corners
        of the plan are stepped.
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    - 'Facts and Details - Borobudur: History, Architecture, Components (factsanddetails.com)'
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (01-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: pemugaran
    partName: Teras4
    localPosition: {x: 20, y: 1.7999992, z: -43.249996}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Penemuan & Pemugaran
      en: Rediscovery & Restoration
    regionalTerm: 
    material:
      id: "Batu andesit (seluruh candi \xB155.000 m\xB3)"
      en: "Andesite stone (\xB155,000 m\xB3 for the whole temple)"
    philosophy:
      id: 'Borobudur tetap menjadi tempat ibadah yang hidup: setiap tahun saat Waisak
        (purnama Mei atau Juni), umat Buddha Indonesia berjalan mengelilingi candi
        searah jarum jam (pradaksina) dan bermeditasi.'
      en: 'Borobudur remains a living place of worship: every year at Vesak (the
        full moon in May or June), Indonesian Buddhists walk clockwise around the
        temple (pradakshina) and meditate.'
    craft:
      id: Pemugaran pertama dipimpin Theodoor van Erp pada 1907-1911. Pada pemugaran
        besar 1975-1982 (biaya US$6.901.243), lebih dari satu juta batu dibongkar
        lalu diidentifikasi, dicatat, dan dibersihkan satu per satu seperti kepingan
        puzzle raksasa; fondasi distabilkan dan saluran air ditanam di dalam candi.
      en: The first restoration was led by Theodoor van Erp in 1907-1911. In the
        major 1975-1982 restoration (cost US$6,901,243), over one million stones
        were dismantled, then individually identified, catalogued and cleaned like
        pieces of a giant jigsaw puzzle; the foundation was stabilised and drainage
        channels were embedded in the monument.
    history:
      id: Pada 1814 Thomas Stamford Raffles mengutus insinyur H.C. Cornelius, yang
        bersama 200 orang membersihkan candi dari semak selama dua bulan. Borobudur
        ditetapkan sebagai Warisan Dunia UNESCO pada 1991. Pada 21 Januari 1985 sembilan
        stupa rusak parah akibat bom.
      en: In 1814 Thomas Stamford Raffles sent the engineer H.C. Cornelius, who with
        200 men cleared the temple of vegetation over two months. Borobudur was inscribed
        as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1991. On 21 January 1985 nine stupas were
        badly damaged by bombs.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: Pemugaran pertama dipimpin Theodoor van Erp pada 1907-1911. Pada pemugaran
        besar 1975-1982 (biaya US$6.901.243), lebih dari satu juta batu dibongkar
        lalu diidentifikasi, dicatat, dan dibersihkan satu per satu seperti kepingan
        puzzle raksasa; fondasi distabilkan dan saluran air ditanam di dalam candi.
      en: The first restoration was led by Theodoor van Erp in 1907-1911. In the
        major 1975-1982 restoration (cost US$6,901,243), over one million stones
        were dismantled, then individually identified, catalogued and cleaned like
        pieces of a giant jigsaw puzzle; the foundation was stabilised and drainage
        channels were embedded in the monument.
    sources:
    - 'Model: Blender dari data ukuran bersumber + perkiraan (Tools/blender/candi_borobudur.py,
      Docs/Borobudur_Data.md)'
    - Wikipedia - Borobudur (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur)
    curatorValidated: 0
